        defEn: "Holding your child for the first time. Your identity is irreversibly rewritten in one second — from now on you're not just you, you're someone's parent.",
        core: "A面：成为父母是一种最彻底的身份扩展——你的世界突然多了一个比你自己更重要的人。这种重要性不是你选择的，它是一种生物学级别的劫持。/ B面：自由的终结——从此你的每一个决定都不再只关于你。你永远不能再'只为自己活'了。孩子是一根不可切断的绳索——它把你绑在了一个你无法离开的未来上。关键张力：你爱他——但这种爱是你选择的，还是基因植入的？ | 实在界入侵(Tuche): 父母之爱不是一种选择——它是一种劫持。你的身体在你的意识同意之前就已经决定了：这个小东西比你的命重要。",
        coreEn: "A-side: Becoming a parent is the most thorough identity expansion — your world suddenly has someone more important than yourself. This importance isn't chosen, it's a biological-level hijacking. / B-side: End of freedom — from now on every decision isn't just about you. You can never 'live only for yourself' again. The child is an unseverable rope tying you to an inescapable future. Key tension: You love them — but is this love your choice, or a genetic implant? | Real punctured: Parental love is not a choice — it's a hijacking. Your body decided before your consciousness agreed: this small thing matters more than your life.",
        reference: "《美丽人生》中父亲为保护儿子在集中营中编织谎言的圭多；《佛罗里达乐园》中底层母亲用尽一切保护女儿童年的莫妮。",
        referenceEn: "Guido weaving lies in a concentration camp to protect his son in Life Is Beautiful; Mooni the destitute mother doing everything to protect her daughter's childhood in The Florida Project.",

        topology: "身份的生物学劫持：你的身体在你同意之前就决定了这个小东西比你的命重要",

